Unreal Gold port: SDLDrv for a single-surface handheld (muOS, RG34XX-SP).

Applies to SDLDrv/ from OldUnreal-UnrealPatch227k-SDK-Linux.tar.bz2
(v227k_15) with `patch -p1 -F0` run in the directory containing SDLDrv/.
No class layout changes: USDLClient and USDLViewport keep the size and
field offsets of the official 227k_15 SDLDrv.so (checked by abi_check.cpp).

Always on:
- UpdateInput ignores SDL window events whose windowID is not the
  viewport's window. Stock SDLDrv applied the launcher splash window's and
  the renderers' hidden probe windows' size changes to the viewport.
- SetMouseCapture logs when the stock path changes the capture state.

Only when UNREALGOLD_HANDHELD is set to anything but "" or "0" (read once
in USDLClient::Init into GSDLDrvHandheld):
- Software menu cursor: bWindowsMouseAvailable stays 0 and the mouse stays
  grabbed in relative mode, so UWindow draws its own cursor from
  IK_MouseX/IK_MouseY. SetMouseCapture does nothing while that holds
  (UGameEngine::Tick calls it every tick while a menu is open). The
  UWindow cursor is centred whenever a menu opens.
- Fullscreen only: the window is created fullscreen; no SetWindowSize,
  SetWindowPosition, SetWindowFullscreenMode or RaiseWindow; EndFullscreen
  (Alt+Enter, TOGGLEFULLSCREEN, ENDFULLSCREEN, failed SETRES) and
  SetScreenMode Windowed/Borderless are logged no-ops; SETRES, TEMPSETRES
  and the startup render device always ask for fullscreen.
- RELAUNCH is swallowed (it would fork/exec a second game process onto the
  single fbdev surface); the player is told to restart instead.

Text input stays off (SDL_StartTextInput remains compiled out), so a
digit key still types exactly one character.

